# Personal figures — plan cost, credit balance, renewal date.
# Everything the API cannot see lives here, which is precisely why it is private.
# Copy plan.example.json -> plan.json and fill it in; the app runs fine without it
# (the declared tiles simply disappear).
plan.json

# Workspace glue: an @-import pointing into a private Obsidian vault.
# Machine-specific, not part of the app. All three agent adapters point at the
# same private state — GEMINI.md leaked into a public commit once (2026-08-18,
# v1.7.1) before this line existed; it is why this comment is this explicit.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md

# Local agent plans and project-working adapters are not public product source.
agents/

# Machine-local launcher glue and its output. These carry absolute paths for one
# specific device (drive letters, node install location, user profile). They are how
# Matra is started on that machine, not how the app works, so they are not product
# source. Added 2026-08-23: all three sat untracked and un-ignored, one `git add -A`
# away from a public commit - the same gap that put GEMINI.md on the remote in v1.7.1.
start-matra.ps1
_make-shortcut.ps1
server.log

# Build artifacts — the .vsix is produced by `npm run package`, attach it to a
# GitHub Release rather than committing a binary on every version bump.
*.vsix
node_modules/
dist/
.desktop-test/
upstream-codenotch/
native/target/

.DS_Store
